## 2026-05-24 — Travel-to-adventure and recovered-treasure XP hook

### Gap found during continuation audit

After hook choice, the prototype still needed the first actual expedition step and a stronger XP/progression receipt. The campaign could choose a lead, but it did not yet spend travel time, consume supplies, roll travel checks, move the party to the chosen adventure site, or show XP changing on the monitor.

### Source receipts

Added wilderness travel and XP receipts to [[resources/ose-session-zero-source-receipts]]:

- `old-school-essentials-classic-fantasy-rules-tome-3751c5149a24:s557` — wilderness day sequence: decide course, losing direction, wandering monsters, description, end-of-day rations/time/rest
- `old-school-essentials-classic-fantasy-rules-tome-3751c5149a24:s563` — losing direction chances by terrain
- `old-school-essentials-classic-fantasy-rules-tome-3751c5149a24:s570` / `s571` — wandering monster checks and settled/clear `1-in-6`
- `old-school-essentials-classic-fantasy-rules-tome-3751c5149a24:s709` / `s710` / `s711` — XP from recovered treasure and defeated monsters; non-magical treasure gives `1 XP` per `1 gp` value

### Implemented

Added domain/runtime support for the first expedition step:

- `travelToChosenHook(campaign, randomInt)`
  - requires a chosen hook
  - rolls OSE-style losing direction check for a settled/clear route
  - rolls OSE-style wandering encounter check
  - rolls encounter distance as `4d6 × 10` yards when an encounter appears
  - consumes a travel day of rations or harms unfed characters
  - advances time to the next morning
  - moves party/characters to the chosen destination
- `/api/travel-to-adventure`
- monitor button: `Travel to adventure`

Added a minimal progression hook:

- `awardRecoveredTreasureXp(campaign, treasureGp, reason)`
- `/api/recover-demo-treasure`
- monitor now shows character XP

