## 2026-05-24 — Browser-tested monitor loading fix and honest controls

### Bug

Joel tested the deployed monitor and it hung at `Loading...`. Root cause: the Worker embeds monitor JavaScript inside a template literal, and the source used string literals like `'\\n\\n'`. Inside the generated HTML those became literal newlines inside quoted JavaScript strings, which broke the browser script. `curl` still returned a 200 page, so the prior smoke was fake comfort.

### Fix

- Replaced embedded newline literals with `String.fromCharCode(10)` / `blankLine` in the monitor script.
- Added the project rule to `.pi/APPEND_SYSTEM.md`: browser-test deployed monitor/UI with agent-browser before claiming it works.
- Preserved `campaign=<id>` query parameters for `/api/*`, `/events`, and `/events-dev`, so browser test runs are isolated and button clicks update the same campaign shown on screen.
- Split public vs dev controls:
  - public shows only honest flow buttons: reset, PlayerAgent Session 0, PlayerAgent hook choice, dice/procedure travel, faction clocks
  - demo scaffold buttons are hidden unless `?dev=1`
- Added an explicit note on the monitor: Kimi creates character plans / hook choices; deterministic Referee code resolves typed choices with dice/procedure.

### Deploy receipt

```txt
agentdungeon.ai (custom domain)
Current Version ID: edddb1bb-7e8a-4b18-a42f-8dccc7076720
```

